@host = http://localhost:5001
@tenant = acme

### Building history. Change the tenant to northstar and repeat.

GET {{host}}/buildings
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}

###

GET {{host}}/invoices?buildingId=101
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}

###

GET {{host}}/invoices/501
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}

### Follow a line to its asset.

GET {{host}}/assets/11
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}

### Filter the building's invoices to its previous owner.

GET {{host}}/invoices?buildingId=101&customerId=8
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}

### Create a draft invoice.

# @name draft
POST {{host}}/invoices
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "buildingId": 101,
  "currency": "PLN",
  "lines": [
    { "assetId": 11, "description": "Lift inspection", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 150 }
  ]
}

### Add a second asset to the draft.

POST {{host}}/invoices/{{draft.response.body.$.id}}/lines
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assetId": 12, "description": "Ventilation service", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 75 }

### Verify the draft has two lines and totals 375 PLN.

GET {{host}}/invoices/{{draft.response.body.$.id}}
X-Tenant: {{tenant}}

### Missing tenant (400).

GET {{host}}/buildings

### Invoice 502 belongs to Acme (404 for Northstar).

GET {{host}}/invoices/502
X-Tenant: northstar

###

GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

###

GET {{host}}/necto/endpoint-mappings
